@@ -5,5 +5,23 @@ an alert to a Slack channel when an access request is created. You can find the
 Teleport Access API in the main Teleport repository and the Slack access request
 plugin in `github.com/gravitational/teleport/integrations/access/slack`.
 
+## Beams-enabled container
+
+`Dockerfile.beams` builds both `teleport-slack` and a matching `tsh` binary so
+the `/beams` command does not depend on tools installed on the host. Per-user
+Teleport profiles are stored in `/var/lib/teleport-slack/beams`; mount this path
+on persistent encrypted storage so users do not need to reconnect after every
+container restart.
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```console
+docker compose -f integrations/access/slack/docker-compose.beams.yml up --build
+```
+
+The image runs as UID/GID `10001`, drops all Linux capabilities in the Compose
+example, and only needs outbound access to Slack and configured Teleport
+tenants.
+
 If you have a self-hosted Teleport deployment, you can find information for
 configuring this access request plugin in [Access Requests with Slack](https://goteleport.com/docs/access-controls/access-request-plugins/ssh-approval-slack/).
